# Keep line endings deterministic regardless of each contributor's
# core.autocrlf. Without this, a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true smudges
# files to CRLF on checkout.
#
# Repo-wide default: let Git auto-detect text vs binary, and check out every
# text file with LF. The whole tree is already LF in the index, so this
# normalizes with zero churn while protecting future files (and this file
# itself) from CRLF smudging.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders for the scripts where CRLF actually breaks execution: a
# CRLF shebang ("#!/usr/bin/env bash\r") fails to exec on Linux/WSL/macOS with a
# "bad interpreter" error. PowerShell reads LF cleanly on both 5.1 and 7.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=lf
